					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-388715#post-4721449</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-388715/transcript-of-dr-clef-s-seminar-reality-benders-and-you:how#post-4721449</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2020 20:39:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>AFX Neuromancer</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>2739221</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm hesitant to make any edits to an article with over a thousand positive votes, even a simple edit, but I just wanted to point out a punctuation error that occurs throughout. Each paragraph shouldn't have a quotation mark at the end. Since it's the same person talking, the only paragraph that should have a closing quotation mark at the end is the very last paragraph. However, each paragraph <em>should</em> have the opening quotation mark in the beginning, that's done correctly.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-388715#post-4619873</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-388715/transcript-of-dr-clef-s-seminar-reality-benders-and-you:how#post-4619873</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 28 Apr 2020 19:27:17 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>SharpEmbrace</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>6032914</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm curious. What about this is funny? I feel like I'm missing something, as this seems to be more horrifying than comedic to me. It tries to exemplify the feeling of powerlessness in the face of a merciless god, which I don't find amusing. Some of Clef's lines indicate he finds it funny, but I think they are intended to convey that, in the eyes of a Type Green, humans are nothing but playthings to laugh at until they get bored and slaughter them. The implications are pretty grim.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
